    [Performance][Kernel] Optimize hc_pre kernels/main (#18293)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it
    
    Integrate an optimized `hc_pre` operator implementation for evaluation
    on Ascend A3. The operator source was adapted from the
    [cann-recipes-infer
    implementation](https://gitcode.com/renruhai/cann-recipes-infer/tree/master/ops/ascendc/src/hc_pre).
    
    The changes are limited to the operator implementation and its build
    integration. They also include a follow-up HF32 mode fix. The Python API
    and model call sites are unchanged. This PR does not claim an A5
    performance improvement.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce any user-facing change?
    
    There is no change to the inputs or outputs for supported
    configurations.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Built and installed the custom operator on Ascend A3.
    - Ran the existing single-card `hc_pre` correctness tests after the HF32
    fix: 5 passed.
    - Compared pre-optimization commit `cc06c1e5` with fixed optimized
    commit `648d8b6d` on the same Ascend910_9382 host using GLM-5.3-Flash
    W8A8. The `hc_pre` source at `648d8b6d` matches this PR. The figures are
    median `HcPre` device durations from the same DP0/TP0 rank.
    
    | Capture | Input shape | Calls per version | Baseline | Optimized |
    Change |
    | --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
    | Prefill | `[432, 4, 4096]` | 90 | 112.758 μs | 68.919 μs | −38.9% |
    | Prefill | `[80, 4, 4096]` | 90 | 48.709 μs | 41.859 μs | −14.1% |
    | Prefill | `[1, 4, 4096]` | 90 | 29.469 μs | 31.170 μs | +5.8% |
    | Decode | `[2, 4, 4096]` | 1,890 | 37.090 μs | 34.130 μs | −8.0% |
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c4df37dfcc7f72ca41cd43801a468526ecf99a2b
    
